Package: luna-media-player
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, libgtk-3-0, libglib2.0-0, libmpv2 | libmpv1
Description: XP-era music and video player for the Linux desktop
 Luna Media Player plays the music and video already on your machine,
 wrapped in the look of the desktop players of 2004: a library with tag
 reading and search, a Now Playing list, and eight flowing visualisations.
 .
 Playback is handled by libmpv, so it opens essentially any format your
 system can decode — MP3, FLAC, WAV, OGG, Opus, AAC, M4A and WMA, as well
 as MP4, MKV, AVI, WebM, MOV and WMV. Files and folders open from the file
 manager or the command line.
 .
 Published by Dhiva-Labs.
